    "title": "Fire in 35-story Manhattan apartment building claims one life: officials - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Mitchell Zhané Caldwell ,\n3 hours ago\nEAST HARLEM, Manhattan (PIX11) — A person has died after a fire broke out at a 35-story apartment building in East Harlem on Wednesday evening, according to the NYPD.\nThe fire was reported around 6:59 p.m. at 221 East 112th Street.\nMore Local News Firefighters responded to the 19th floor, where the fire broke out. The fire was under control around 8:06 p.m.\nA 72-year-old woman died, police say. Two firefighters were taken to a local hospital with injuries.\nOne man who was in the apartment building at the time of the fire says the smoke was overpowering. “The smoke was intense. I felt the fire next door. I couldn’t breathe.”\n“The smoke was intense. I felt the fire next door because I tried to help out the guy the smoke, it’s too overpowering, it was too overpowering. Couldn’t breathe.”\nFire officials are investigating the cause of the fire.\nBen Mitchell is a digital content producer from Vermont who has covered both local and international news since 2021. He joined PIX11 in 2024. See more of his work here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to PIX11.",
